  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to formalisation of the economy including social protection and support to PFM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Action will support the expansion and strengthen the sustainability of Angola&#xbf;s economic formalization program. To promote the transition to formality, the Government of Angola (GoA) launched in 2020 the Informal Economy Conversion Programme (PREI, Programa de Reconvers&#xe3;o da Economia Informal) a multi-sectorial programme supported by an EU&#xbf;s Budget Support 2020-22 (first disbursement in 2021 and second and last disbursement expected in 2022). To date, a small-scale though relatively successful formalisation campaign has focused on a simplified registration process followed by some immediate benefits (trainings, and access to mobile money and microcredits). To that end, legal provisions have been enacted, allowing for: i) fast-track municipal registration for vendors; ii) &#xbf;one stop-shop&#xbf; for the creation of small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) and iii) low income self-employees registration to the National Institute for Social This Action aims at strengthening the viability and sustainability of the ambitioned scale-up of PREI&#xbf;s results and expansion to Angola&#xbf;s 18 provinces. The proposal is to help the authorities design a sustainable &#xbf;one-stop shop&#xbf;, or integrated administration service closer to the centres of informal economic activity, jointly with simplified procedures and lower transition costs. The Action also seeks to expand access to social protection, financial services and business-related training for vulnerable workers and businesses. Specifically, with this Sector Reform Performance Contract, EU will provide financial transfers (EUR 45 Million) and technical assistance (including through the International Labour Organization (ILO)) as well as conduct inclusive policy dialogue towards defining a government plan to ensure sustainable formalisation and achieving continuous progress in accelerating the formalization process, along with social benefits (access to social protection) and financial inclusion of formalized workers.Through this Action, the EU will also support the implementation of stability-oriented macro-economic policies and Public Finance Management (PFM) reforms, through a blending operation of EUR 5 Million which will support the disbursement of Budget Support tranches. The on-going Public Expenditure and Fiscal Accountability (PEFA) assessment will guide the Government&#xbf;s strategy on the PFM Reform Action Plan and on bolstering the mobilization of domestic revenues. The PFM blending operation will top up a EUR 200 Million loan by AFD combined with a grant of EUR 2.6 million, to support the Government&#xb4;s PFM reform agenda in three areas: i) PFM and transparency of public administration; ii) governance of the State-owned Enterprises (SOEs) and Public Private Partnerships (PPPs); and iii) inclusiveness and sustainability of the financial sector.</narrative>
  </description>
